  "body": "Currently the HTML standard for autocomplete attritube does not provide feature detection, which means fields are really supported by browser. This is useful for developers and websites if some fields aren't supported, it can treat it as autocomplete=\"off\", or they can test this field before adding to autocomplete attritube. Now, autocomplete attritube is  parsing and returning autocomplete field names, which aren't really useful. Suggest adding a feature detection for autocomplete attritube, if some fields aren't supported, it returns \"\".\r\n\r\n\r\n@mnoorenberghe, @vabr-g  ",
